gmlx is pure Python. Most third-party code arrives as installed
dependencies, each under its own license: mlx-kquant (MIT; supplies the
K-quant Metal kernels and the C++ GGUF reader, with its own attributions to
MLX, ggml/llama.cpp, and gguf-tools), MLX and mlx-lm (MIT, Copyright ©
Apple Inc.), mlx-vlm (MIT, Copyright © Prince Canuma), and the GGUF file
format defined by the ggml/llama.cpp project (MIT, Copyright (c) Georgi
Gerganov).

Some third-party code is vendored or adapted into the gmlx tree, and that
code keeps its project's license. Each such source file states its
provenance in its header. The licenses/ directory, which every gmlx
distribution includes, reproduces each project's license with the files
that carry its code, and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md summarizes what was used
from each project:

- misaki (Apache License 2.0, Copyright © hexgrad): a snapshot vendored at
  gmlx/_vendor/misaki (see gmlx/_vendor/misaki/LICENSE and
  licenses/misaki-LICENSE), which itself incorporates components adapted
  from g2pK and PaddleSpeech as noted in its subdirectory READMEs.
- mlx-lm (MIT, Copyright © Apple Inc.): licenses/mlx-lm-LICENSE.
- mlx-vlm (MIT, Copyright © Prince Canuma): licenses/mlx-vlm-LICENSE.
- omlx (Apache License 2.0, Copyright (c) the omlx contributors):
  licenses/omlx-LICENSE.
- ds4.c (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 The ds4.c authors):
  licenses/ds4.c-LICENSE.
- The DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731 reference inference code (MIT, Copyright (c)
  2023 DeepSeek): licenses/deepseek-v4-LICENSE.
- llama.cpp and ggml (MIT, Copyright (c) The ggml authors):
  licenses/llama.cpp-LICENSE.
- beellama.cpp (MIT, Copyright (c) The ggml authors, Anbeeld):
  licenses/beellama.cpp-LICENSE.
- vLLM (Apache License 2.0, Copyright contributors to the vLLM project):
  licenses/vllm-LICENSE.
- The OpenJev helper (Apache License 2.0): licenses/openjev-LICENSE, which
  also reproduces the OpenJev repository's NOTICE.
- system-one-adapter-python (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 TypeSafe AI):
  licenses/system-one-adapter-LICENSE.

